      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>A conveyor looks safe until it jams. Then people are tempted to reach in. Locking off takes longer. That is how people lose arms and lives. A good inspection checks the guards, the pull-cord and the lock-off before the belt runs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Most injuries happen at nip points, and when clearing a blockage on a belt that was not isolated.</li><li>Check three things: fixed guards, a working pull-cord, and safe lock-off.</li><li>Conveyors are work equipment under PUWER 1998. Quarries also fall under the Quarries Regulations 1999.</li><li>Lock off before anyone reaches in. Switched off is not enough.</li><li>The checklist does not make the conveyor safe. The record is what an HSE inspector asks to see.</li></ul>"
    },
