      "heading": "Guarding at trapping points",
      "html": "<p>The classic injury is a hand or sleeve pulled in where the belt meets a drum or roller. Fixed guards belong at every trapping point. That means head and tail drums, snub and bend pulleys, return rollers, tensioners and transfers. Guards must be in place, secure and not bypassed.</p><p>Check each guard. Take a photo of any that is missing, loose or bypassed. Quickler records it point by point. It records the guard. It does not replace it.</p>"
