      "html": "<p>A pull-cord runs the whole length. Anyone can stop the belt from any point. The cord must be there along the whole run, tight, connected, and it must stop the drive when you test it. A slack or cut cord looks fine and does nothing.</p><p>Walk the run. Test the cord. Send a photo of any slack or broken part. Quickler records the result against the conveyor. Follow your site's way of testing and resetting.</p>"
